'' A WIDE SELECT SUBJECT'S TEMPORARIES DIE ON EVERY WAY OUT OF THE SELECT.
''
'' They were on the statement-wide list, which only sel.join flushed, so a RETURN or an
'' EXIT out of a case skipped them: 'select case "a" & wstr( k )' in a function returning
'' from its case leaked the chain on every call. They are now the SELECT's own scope --
'' CLEANUP_WSTR_DELETE entries -- which sel.join closes and every RETURN and EXIT runs.
'' Measured, fbc deletes its subject on the return path before its 'goto' to the exit.
''
'' And the scalar 'wstr( i )' inside the chain was never deleted at all, in any
'' statement: LowerWstrOf's number row called EmitRtl and dropped the pointer, where
'' every string row beside it went through WideConcatStep_. 'print "a" & wstr( i )'
'' is fbc's two fb_WstrDelete and was one.
''
'' The golden pins WHERE each fb_WstrDelete goes: both before each 'ret' out of a case,
'' both before the 'br for.exit4' of the EXIT FOR, both at sel.join. Run 3,000,000
'' times, the peak working set is 4.39 MB at 300,000 and at 3,000,000 iterations.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/select-wide-subject-cleanup.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrDelete(
'' GOLDEN: expected/select-wide-subject-cleanup.out
